Congratulations, you have found one of the spectacular bugs/features of 
Nethack.  Something strange happens when monsters pick up gold.  If a pet
picks up some gold, every time it picks up and then drops another object,
it also drops all of the gold it carries WHILE SIMULTANEOUSLY RETAINING THE
GOLD!  So, the more money your pet ogre carries, the faster you can make
money.  There is a limit, though.  If your pet carries more than 10,000 
gold pieces, he will still drop only 10,000, give or take a few hundred.

This works with all pets who are interested in money, as far as I have 
determined.  The list includes dwarves, orcs of all kinds, including orc
captains, shamans, mummies and zombies, centaurs of all kinds, dragons of all 
kinds, all kinds of Ogres including zombies and mummies, and I suppose 
leprechauns, although I've never tried them.

Here's an interesting point, though, your pet will never pick up gold once
he becomes your pet, so you have to figure another way to make him rich.

You don't need to have pets, though.  Any monster interested in gold can
make you richer.  Give them all your money, then kill them and take it 
back.  Like Jesus throwing loaves of bread upon the water, it will come
back with interest.  But again, the rule of 10,000 applies.  If you give
a monster more than 10,000 gold pieces, you won't get back much more than
10,000.  

So remember, don't leave 10,000,000,000,000 gold pieces lying around for a 
dwarf to wander by and pick up, you won't like what happens.

